# Tvara Global Rules

**Authority:** `AGENTS.md` is the authoritative contract. `THEME_MAP.md` is the file registry. These rules reinforce both — they do not override them.

## Before any task

1. Read `AGENTS.md` (RPI protocol).
2. Read `THEME_MAP.md` for every file you will touch.
3. Wait for explicit approval before implementing (Phase 2 of RPI).

## Non-negotiables (from AGENTS.md)

- No CDN URLs — all JS/CSS/fonts served from `assets/`.
- Cart AJAX via `Alpine.store('cart')` in `theme-state.js` only — no direct `fetch('/cart/...')` in components.
- Alpine stores for reactive state — no `querySelector` to sync cart/UI state.
- Non-trivial JS in paired `assets/*.js` (Custom Elements); minimal few-line inline `<script>` in sections/snippets is OK per `AGENTS.md` §5b.
- Never `DOMContentLoaded` — inline script after markup, or Custom Element `connectedCallback`.
- CSS tokens in `snippets/css-variables.liquid` — no Liquid in `assets/*.css`.
- `@font-face` only in `layout/theme.liquid` — `.woff2` only.
- Update `THEME_MAP.md` after every file create/rename/delete (part of the task).

## Naming

- Sections: `sections/{name}.liquid` — no `main-` prefix.
- Snippets: `snippets/component-{name}.liquid`.
- Assets: `assets/section-{name}.js|css` or `assets/component-{name}.js|css`.
- BEM class names matching the component block name.
